ue ""} "Athletics in other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "74"} "1859 Zappas Olympic Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "75"} "1870 Zappas Olympic Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "76"} "1875 Zappas Olympic Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "77"} "1888-89 Zappas Olympic Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "1"} "1896 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "2"} "1900 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "3"} "1904 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "4"} "1906  Intercalated Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "5"} "1908 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "6"} "1912 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "7"} "1920 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "8"} "1924 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "9"} "1928 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "10"} "1932 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "11"} "1936 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "12"} "1948 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "13"} "1952 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "14"} "1956 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "15"} "1960 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "16"} "1964 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "17"} "1968 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "18"} "1972 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "19"} "1976 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "20"} "1980 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "21"} "1984 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "22"} "1988 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "23"} "1992 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "24"} "1996 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "25"} "2000 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "26"} "2004 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "53"} "2008 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "65"} "2010 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "54"} "2012 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "67"} "2014 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "69"} "2018 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "61"} "2020 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "63"} "2024 Summer Olympics"]]] [:script {} "$('#sport_in_other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/' + $('#sport_in_other_games_select').val() + '/sports/ATH'})"] "\n" [:h1 {} "Athletics at the 2016 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:table {:class "biodata"} "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Dates"] "\n" [:td {} "12 – 21 August 2016"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Medal Events"] "\n" [:td {} "47"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Venues"] "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/909"} "Estádio Olímpico João Havelange, Engenho de Dentro, Rio de Janeiro"] " / " [:a {:href "/venues/910"} "Sambódromo, Rio de Janeiro"] " / " [:a {:href "/venues/925"} "Praia do Pontal, Recreio dos Bandeirantes, Rio de Janeiro"]] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "Controversy enveloped the 2016 Olympic athletics competition as far back as late 2015. At that time a German television network released a documentary alleging systematic doping in Russia. After investigations by the IAAF, the entire Russian athletic team was suspended from international competition early in 2016. Then, only a few weeks before the Rio Olympics began, an independent report commissioned by WADA, the McLaren Report, corroborated these findings, and many Russian athletes in other sports, notably rowing, were also suspended. The IOC had to quickly rule on this report, and supported it, but allowed some individual Russian athletes to compete after they had been cleared by their federations. For the Russians track &amp; field athletes, this would be only one competitor, female long jumper " [:a {:href "/athletes/131561"} "Darya Klishina"] ", who had lived and trained in the United States for the past few years and had been subjected to multiple drug tests."] "\n\n" [:p {} "With this negative background the biggest positive story of Rio athletics was Jamaican wunder-sprinter " [:a {:href "/athletes/105512"} "Usain Bolt"] ", who was trying to win his third consecutive sprint triple with golds in the 100 metres, 200 metres, and 4x100 metre relay. It was a quest at which he would be successful in Rio, giving him nine Olympic gold medals, equaling the Olympic record for athletics held by " [:a {:href "/athletes/67728"} "Paavo Nurmi"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/78692"} "Carl Lewis"] " (trailing the 10 of " [:a {:href "/athletes/78385"} "Ray Ewry"] " if one includes the 1906 Olympics)."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Three world records were set in Rio, two by women and one in men’s competition. Ethiopian " [:a {:href "/athletes/130029"} "Almaz Ayana"] " shattered the women’s world mark in the 10,000 metres, Poland’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/115098"} "Anita Włodarczyk"] " broke her own world record in the hammer throw, and South African " [:a {:href "/athletes/135688"} "Wayde van Niekerk"] " broke " [:a {:href "/athletes/78616"} "Michael Johnson"] "’s 17-year old mark in the men’s 400 metres."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The United States would dominate the athletics competition in Rio, winning 32 medals, 16 by the men and 16 by the women. They also led the gold medal lists, winning 13 gold, 7 by men, and 6 by women. Such was their dominance that they also had the most silver medals and bronze medals for both genders, leading the medal tables in every possible category. Since the advent of women’s Olympic competition in 1928, this had only previously been accomplished at the 1932 Olympics."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/358560"} "100 metres, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "13 – 14 August 2016"] "\n" [:td {} "84"] "\n" [:td {} "57"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/358579"} "200 metres, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "16 – 18 August 2016"] "\n" [:td {} "77"] "\n" [:td {} "48"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {}